==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Pai-Pai Z''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Pai-Pai DX''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Pai-Pai is one of the best units in the game against [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] enemies, asserting absolute dominance by taking only 1/4~1/5 damage and dealing 3~4x damage against said trait, depending on how many of the [[Blood Fruit]] [[Treasure]] you have activated. You can also combine her with a tank like [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sushi Cat]] or [[Cat Machine (Uber Rare Cat)|Cat Machine]] to dominate Red enemies.

Pai-Pai can almost guarantee victory in [[Realm of Carnage (Deadly)|Realm of Carnage]] and [[Wrath of Carnage (Deadly)|Wrath of Carnage]], because she can easily punch through the Reds while being weaken immune. Just make sure to take out the [[R.Ost]]s with something else.

Overall, Pai-Pai is a unit well worth your trouble. Any stage with only Red enemies can be obliterated. This is also helped by a quick recharge, but it's worth noting she has quite the long attack rate and, therefore, average DPS outside of Red enemies. She can always fall on her high health, but defending her is necessary.

==='''True Form'''===
Pai-Pai DX gains a faster attack rate and is now Insanely Tough against Reds, thus boosting her both offensively and defensively. This is all there is, a straight power upgrade, but a welcome one, as the stat boost is quite significant.

Pai-Pai DX, thanks to the shorter time between attacks, also becomes a better generalist, although she is still far from the best in that department.

==='''Talents'''===
Since Pai-Pai's use lies all within her attack and HP, upgrading these core abilities should be considered after a heavy investment with [[Catseye]]s, although it's rarely if ever needed.

Slow Immunity is not very useful due to having little applications. [[Professor A.]] is a prime example, but this enemy's not that threatening to Pai-Pai in the first place. Otherwise, this is only ever useful against the likes of [[Croakley]] if you need to get rid of some nasty Reds.

Survive is good to have with her high range as she will keep on dishing out damage for a while, but doesn't open anymore possibilities for its extreme cost too. Meanwhile, the Slow ability is completely useless, as Pai-Pai is meant to directly eliminate Reds through brute force, and a slow effect only hinders her role by keeping Reds out of range, so it rarely comes into play.

